tgs:Interview.TGS_110_JohnRobb a thinkr:Episode, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:createdDate "2026-09-08"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:updatedDate "2026-09-08"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeType thinkr:EpisodeType.Interview ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeSegment tgs:EpisodeSegment.MainShow ;
    skos:prefLabel "John Robb: \"Networked Tribalism, AI, and Asteroids\""@en ;
    skos:definition "Nate's real, direct first conversation with John Robb, military theorist and technology analyst, ranging across AI, information warfare, tribal polarization, and asteroid mining — directly framed by Nate himself as 'an oddball episode' for the show, justified by having personally followed Robb's work for a long time."@en ;
    thinkr:hasHostIntroduction "Today's guest is John Robb, who currently publishes the Global Guerrillas Report, which covers the intersection of war, politics and technology. John served as a tier one special ops in the military, after which he became a popular internet analyst, entrepreneur, and the COO of a software company that open sourced the current RSS standard. John also published the book Brave New War, which was on the subject of the future of warfare. This may appear to be an oddball episode on The Great Simplification, but I've followed John for a long time now and many in my inner circle make an effort to pay attention to what he says. This was a wide-ranging conversation. We discussed AI, augmented reality, information and sense-making, tribal warfare, fictive kinship, and even asteroid mining, which you might guess I am incredibly skeptical of. But I was also skeptical of things he said 20 years ago, which are our current reality."@en ;
    dct:created "2023-12-04"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:issued "2024-02-21"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:subject tgs:Subject.HumanBehavior, tgs:Subject.EconomicsAndMonetary ;
    thinkr:hasHost tgs:Persona.NateHagens ;
    thinkr:hasGuest tgs:Persona.JohnRobb ;
    thinkr:hasCanonicalSource <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com/episode/110-john-robb> ;
    thinkr:hasReplay <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b2n_Jk37cLE> ;
    thinkr:hasTranscript <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/TGS110JohnRobbTranscript.docx.pdf> ;
    dct:references tgs:Organization.GlobalGuerrillasReport, tgs:Work.BraveNewWar, tgs:Interview.TGS_59_JonathanHaidt, tgs:Work.RealityBlind ;
    thinkr:hasDiscussionSummary "Robb directly frames the current information environment through his own real 'three realms of warfare' concept, arguing tribal moral conflict now spreads through networked social platforms the same way open-source insurgency once spread through decentralized guerrilla cells — the underlying network dynamics being structurally similar even though the domains differ. He's real and direct about a genuine concern with AI data ownership: arguing that if data rights had been established correctly from the start, ordinary people would hold real upside participation in the coming 'AI economy' rather than watching a small number of already-wealthy actors capture nearly all of it. A real, direct concept he calls 'fictive kinship' grounds his account of tribal polarization: people increasingly form intense in-group loyalty with distant strangers who share an ideological identity, activating real, direct mirror-neuron-based empathy for in-group members while readily dehumanizing perceived out-groups. Closes on genuine, direct disagreement rather than false consensus: Robb argues humanity's long-term survival requires committing to space development, using the internet's own real, historical bootstrap from a stalled, underfunded 1990s telecom effort into a fully-realized global network within a decade as his model for how a similarly 'irrational' commitment to space could still succeed; Nate directly, honestly states he'd need 'a magic wand' to believe it, while still respecting Robb's track record enough to invite him back for a deeper dive."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Real, further citable material found but NOT built in this pass: Tristan Harris's own real TGS-16 appearance, directly cited, not yet built despite Harris himself already being a built Human in this graph — now the third time this specific gap has surfaced this session. Art Berman (already built) is directly cross-referenced via a real, separate podcast appearance outside this graph's own TGS episode, not a new find. John Boyd and Marshall McLuhan (both real, directly cited historical/intellectual influences, not built)."@en ;
    .


